.git
.github
dist/
/ic11c
/ic11c.exe
/chipgen
/isagen
/nodegen

# What a release verification records when CORPUS_MANIFEST names a file, and the
# replacement `task msys2:lock` writes beside the lock before moving it over.
/corpus-*.txt
/scripts/msys2-ucrt64.lock.new

# Assembly written by redirecting the compiler, which only ever emits to stdout.
/*.ic10

# Coverage profiles. The sanitize step writes the ephemeral profile under a
# suffix and moves it over, so a run that fails between the two leaves one
# behind; matched by prefix for that reason, as .gitignore matches it.
coverage.out
.coverage-ephemeral.out*

# A pattern here is matched against the whole relative path and `*` does not
# cross a separator, so a bare `bin/` would exclude a root-level one and ship
# every nested one. All three of these occur nested: bin and obj under
# tools/prefabreader, left by a local `dotnet build` of the prefab reader, and
# a test binary beside whichever package `go test -c` built it from.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.test

# Core dumps from a crashed test binary, which land beside the package the
# binary was built from and are tens of megabytes each. Matched the way
# .gitignore matches them, by the pid suffix, so that a source file named
# core.something is not.
**/core.[0-9]*

# Scratch space, which nothing in the build reads. The IC10 corpus under
# tmp/ic10-corpus/ is most of its size.
tmp/

# Task's run-state directory, the agent scratch tree and the editor directories.
# None is read by any stage, and all of them otherwise land in /src in every
# build. All four sit at the root, unlike the file macOS leaves in every
# directory it has opened, which is matched at any depth for the reason the bin
# and obj patterns above are.
.task/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.zed
**/.DS_Store

# Decompiled game source a local `task gamesrc` left behind, twenty-seven
# megabytes of it. Every stage that reads a decompile decompiles its own inside
# the build, so none of this is an input; without the exclusion it is copied
# into the context of every image built here.
gamesrc/
